Researchers had thought the big eruptions are created when magnetic field lines[ from] the core of a sun[spot] become tangled and reconnect high in solar atmosphere, or cor[ona]. The new study contradicts that assumption.
X-7 flare[ started] when plasma[ from] below the Sun's surface broke suddenly through.
