This[ is] a dish with very distinct regional variations[.] In Osaka-style[ okonom]iyaki, all the component ingredients are mixed together in a bowl of batter, then spread out on the grill for cooking[.] The Hiroshima version is more complicated and takes longer to prepare, as the chef (not the customer) assembles distinct layers of toppings, vegetables[,] noodles, fried egg and pancake base into the final product[.]
